     <actual value="1.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to the location shift to Kachin, a new local partner with a strong track record and presence in the implementation area had to be sought for. This resulted in the collaboration with KBC. Before the distribution of cash was conducted, Plan organised a series of trainings for staff from KBC and camp-based volunteers. In total, 37 people have received training on topics such as safeguarding, PSHEA, the basic principles of child rights, child protection in emergencies, psychological well-being and psychological first aid, CFS management, CVA assistance and finance- and anti-fraud policies. Through these trainings, KBC&apos;s staff is equipped with essential knowledge and skills that strengthen their competencies and enable them to effectively implement activities as these. Since these acquired skills can also be put in practice in future work, this capacity-building initiative ensures sustainability and improve KBC&apos;s long-term ability to achieve their organisational goals independently.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
